    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 including the new `Cp31Tests` (`coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`) and all 45 tests, with no failures or errors.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `checkDigit` is a read-time derived field on the owner response, computed exactly like the other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.) via the MapStruct mapper \u2014 no new pipeline step or entity column needed.\n\n1. **`CheckDigits.java`** (new, in the `rest/function/common` helper package) \u2014 a `luhnOf(String)` utility computing a single Luhn check digit over the digits in a value, ignoring non-digit separators, mirroring the algorithm the test uses.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (`integer`, 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 imported `CheckDigits` and added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(CheckDigits.luhnOf(owner.getCustomerCode()))\")`, so every owner response computes the digit over the same `customerCode` string it returns.\n\nThe test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts equality against `checkDigit`; since both are derived from `owner.getCustomerCode()` with the identical algorithm, they match.",
